{
  "topic_id": "t-mm-05-015",
  "book_id": "book-mm-05",
  "title": "16. BARRIER METHODS FOR CONTRACEPTION AND STI PREVENTION",
  "source_sha256": "f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605",
  "block_count": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "order": 0,
      "content": "<div class=\"mm-release-marker\" data-mm-release=\"f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605\" data-mm-topic=\"t-mm-05-015\" hidden></div>\n<h2 class=\"mm-heading mm-h2 mm-header-banner\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7330]\" style=\"background-color: #2F5496; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: 700\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: #FFFFFF; font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt'><strong>16. </strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: #FFFFFF; font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt'><strong>BARRIER METHODS FOR CONTRACEPTION AND STI PREVENTION</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='color: #FFFFFF; font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt'><strong> </strong></span></h2>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7331]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Barrier methods include:</strong></span></p>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7332]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Male condoms</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> (latex, non-latex, and </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>deproteinized</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> latex varieties)</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7333]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Female condoms</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> (nitrile or latex)</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7334]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Diaphragms</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> (latex, silicone)</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7335]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Cervical cap</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> (silicone)</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7336]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Dams</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> (latex, non-latex)</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7337]\" style=\"padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Condoms (male and/or female): Men and women requesting condoms should be informed of the efficacy of condoms including their failure rate relative to other methods.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7338]\" style=\"padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Diaphragms and caps: A diaphragm or cervical cap can be inserted with spermicide any time before intercourse. Spermicide should be reapplied if sex is to take place and the diaphragm or cap has been in situ for &gt;3 hours or if sex is repeated with the m</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>ethod in place. A diaphragm or ce</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>rvical cap should not be removed until at least 6 hours after the last episode of intercourse.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7339]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u21e8</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Barrier Methods at Preventing Transmission of STIs and other infections</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7340]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Condoms recommended</span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Sexually active men and women can be informed that the consistent and correct use of condoms (including with sex toys) is the most efficient means of protecting against HIV and other STIs.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7341]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>HIV</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7342]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Chlamydia trachomatis</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7343]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Neisseria gonorrhoeae</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7344]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Trichomonas vaginalis</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7345]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Syphilis</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7346]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Human papillomavirus</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7347]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Herpes simplex infection</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7348]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Viral hepatitis</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7349]\" style=\"padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u21e8</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Factors Affecting the Efficacy of Barrier Methods</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7350]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Spermicides:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Women using a diaphragm or cap should be advised to use the device with spermicide. The use of condoms lubricated with </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>N-9</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> is </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>not recommended</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7351]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Lubricants:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>When using lubricant with latex condoms, diaphragms, and caps, a </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>water- or silicone-based preparation is recommended</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7352]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Size and shape:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Ill-fitting condoms can be associated with </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>breakage and incomplete use</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7353]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Legal issues:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Health professionals should keep up to date with the important legal issues regarding HIV/STI transmission and advise patients appropriately as regards partner notification, disclosure and condom use.</strong></span></span></div>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7354]\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8pt\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><u><strong>Considerations Following Barrier Method Failure:</strong></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7355]\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8pt\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Emergency contraception (EC)</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> may be indicated in the following situations:</span></p>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7356]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Diaphragm or cap is dislodged or removed within 6 hours of sex</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7357]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Diaphragm has been left in for longer than 3 hours before sex</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> and no additional spermicide applied</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7358]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Condom splitting/breaking</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7359]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Condom slippage</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7360]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Failure to use condoms as advised when starting or switching contraception</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7361]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2022</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>If enzyme-inducing drugs are being used alongside hormonal contraception</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> (combined hormonal contraception, POP and implant) </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>and condoms are not used during or for 28 days after</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7362]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u21e8</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Post-exposure prophylaxis for HIV:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Men and women can be made aware of </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>PEPSE</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>.</span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>For women living with HIV or at high risk of HIV infection, the use of either a diaphragm or cervical cap is a UKMEC Category 3.</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7363]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u21e8</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Post-exposure prophylaxis for HIV:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Men and women can be made aware of </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>PEPSE</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>.</span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>For women living with HIV or at high risk of HIV infection, the use of either a diaphragm or cervical cap is a UKMEC Category 3.</strong></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7364]\" style=\"padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u21e8</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Latex allergy:</strong></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Women with sensitivity to latex proteins should </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>avoid the use of latex barrier contraceptives</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> and may use a:</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7365]\" style=\"padding-left: 72pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">o</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>silicone diaphragm</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7366]\" style=\"padding-left: 72pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">o</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>cervical cap</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7367]\" style=\"padding-left: 72pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">o</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>non-latex male or female condoms</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7368]\" style=\"padding-left: 72pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">o</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>deproteinized</span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> latex male condoms</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7369]\" style=\"padding-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u21e8</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><u><strong>Toxic shock syndrome (TSS):</strong></u></span><br><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>For women with a history of toxic shock syndrome:</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7370]\" style=\"padding-left: 72pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">o</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>The use of the diaphragm, cervical cap or contraceptive sponge is a UKMEC Category 3.</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mm-para mm-list-item\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7371]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; padding-left: 72pt\"><span class=\"mm-list-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">o</span><span class=\"mm-list-body\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>Women with a history of TSS may use male or female condoms.</strong></span></span></div>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7372]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; margin-left: 36pt\"><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>Caps and diaphragms should </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>not be left in situ</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'> for longer than recommended by the manufacturer or </span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'><strong>used during menstruation</strong></span><span class=\"mm-run\" style='font-family: \"Calibri\", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt'>.</span></p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7373]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; margin-left: 36pt\">\u00a0</p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7374]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; margin-left: 36pt\">\u00a0</p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7375]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; margin-left: 36pt\">\u00a0</p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7376]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; margin-left: 36pt\">\u00a0</p>\n<p class=\"mm-para\" data-mm-source-path=\"word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7377]\" style=\"margin-top: 5pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; margin-left: 36pt\">\u00a0</p>",
